menu "Badge Sync Station"

    config SYNC_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Network the station joins to reach the upload endpoint. WPA2-PSK.

    config SYNC_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default ""
        help
            Leave empty for an open network.

    config SYNC_WIFI_STA_MAC
        string "Custom WiFi STA MAC (xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx, empty = chip default)"
        default ""
        help
            Override the WiFi station MAC, e.g. for a MAC-whitelisted IoT
            network. Empty means keep the chip efuse MAC. Applied with
            esp_wifi_set_mac() before wifi start.

            The ID-derived MAC (sync-01 -> 24:0A:C4:C8:46:B2,
            sync-02 -> 24:0A:C4:C8:46:B3) takes precedence over this.

    config SYNC_UPLOAD_URL
        string "HackerAPI badge upload endpoint"
        default "https://api.hackthenorth.com/v3/badge-data/upload"
        help
            The station extracts the claim ID and badge token from the HTNSYNC1
            envelope and POSTs credentials plus its snapshot as JSON parameters
            to this fixed destination.
            For local testing use your Mac's LAN address, not localhost (which
            would point at the station itself). Never send credentials to a
            request-capture service.

    config SYNC_AUTH_TOKEN
        string "Raw station password for the upload endpoint"
        default ""
        help
            Sent as the JSON password parameter. An empty value disables uploads. Use the raw station password supplied separately
            by the maintainer, not HackerAPI badgeUploadPasswordHash. Keep
            the raw value outside source control.

            Note this is compiled into the image and readable from a flash dump.
            It authenticates the station to the server; it is not a secret that
            survives someone walking off with the hardware.

    config SYNC_MAC_DERIVE_ENABLE
        bool "Derive WiFi STA MAC from station id (sync-01 -> B2, sync-02 -> B3)"
        default n
        help
            Overrides the STA MAC with the chip base plus the ID-derived
            last byte. Off while venue debugging: the desk then uses
            SYNC_WIFI_STA_MAC (or the chip MAC when empty) with no runtime
            override.

    config SYNC_STATION_ID
        string "Station id"
        default "sync-01"
        help
            Identifies this station. Broadcast in the body of every idle beacon,
            which is how a badge learns which desk it walked up to. It is local
            radio metadata and is not sent to HackerAPI.

            This is the fallback boot selection: the Up-button ID editor
            steps between sync-01/sync-02 at runtime and the choice persists
            in NVS. Set it to the id for where this desk lives.

            Max 39 characters, to match BBX_MAX_BOX_ID.

    config SYNC_MAX_BLOB_BYTES
        int "Largest snapshot to accept (bytes)"
        default 32768
        range 1024 52785
        help
            An XFER_OPEN declaring more than this is refused with
            BBX_ST_TOO_BIG before anything is allocated, so a badge asking for
            an absurd transfer cannot exhaust the station's heap.

            The protocol ceiling is 52785 (255 frames x 207 B); going above that
            needs a wider seq/total in bbx_proto.h.

    config SYNC_ADV_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Advertising interval during a transfer (ms)"
        default 30
        range 20 1000
        help
            Dropped from the idle 200 ms while a session is live. The station's
            GRANT and STAT frames are round-trip latency for the badge, so this
            is most of what decides how long a sync takes.

            20 ms is the BLE-legal floor for a non-connectable extended
            advertisement. 30 leaves margin.

    config SYNC_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "HTTP request timeout (ms)"
        default 15000
        range 2000 60000
        help
            Covers DNS, TLS and the whole POST. A 20-25 KB body over a busy
            venue AP, with WiFi and BLE sharing the C3's single radio, will
            exceed the relay's 8 s often enough to matter.

    config SYNC_SELFTEST_ON_BOOT
        bool "POST a synthetic snapshot at boot"
        default n
        help
            Sends one generated ~20 KB body to the endpoint during startup and
            logs the result. This is what proves WiFi, DNS, TLS, the chunked
            write loop and the LWIP buffer sizing before any BLE traffic
            exists — the riskiest part of the station, tested with the radio
            uninvolved. Leave disabled against HackerAPI: the synthetic fixture
            has no valid registered claim/token, so the endpoint rejects it.

    config SYNC_LOOPBACK_TEST
        bool "Run the reassembly loopback test at boot"
        default n
        help
            Synthesises an OPEN + DATA sequence for a ~20 KB payload with
            induced frame loss and feeds it straight into the receive path,
            with no badge and no radio involved.

            This is how the bitmap arithmetic gets debugged: LSB-first bit
            order, the short final frame, and the requirement that a repeated
            OPEN not reset a transfer in progress. Those are exactly the bugs
            that are miserable to diagnose over the air.

            Leave off in the field — it consumes a session slot at boot.

    config SYNC_SUPABASE_URL
        string "Supabase URL for heartbeats"
        default "https://qoouxoeavyuokuscvxff.supabase.co"
        help
            Project URL for the 3-minute heartbeat (touch_sync_heartbeat
            RPC). Same project as the relay server's box_decisions table.

    config SYNC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
        string "Supabase anon key for heartbeats"
        default ""
        help
            Publishable anon key (Project Settings -> API). Only used to
            call the touch_sync_heartbeat() RPC; the heartbeat tables
            have no public access. Empty disables the heartbeat task.

    config SYNC_HEARTBEAT_ENABLE
        bool "Send a Supabase heartbeat every 3 minutes"
        default y
        help
            POSTs this station's id to Supabase on a loop. A pg_cron
            watchdog Slacks when a station goes stale (see the _heartbeats
            migration). Needs SUPABASE_ANON_KEY above; without it the
            task exits.

    config SYNC_SCREEN_ENABLE
        bool "LCD status screen (same panel as the badge)"
        default y
        help
            Shows what the station is doing on the badge-family LCD
            (ST7789 320x240 over SPI, rendered with LVGL — the same
            graphics system as the badge). The display is status-only:
            without it the station runs headless and every screen call
            is a no-op.

    config SYNC_AIR_DEBUG
        bool "Show air-traffic counters on the idle screen"
        default n
        help
            Appends heard/total advertisement counts to the idle line so
            the desk can tell a deaf scan apart from a quiet room. Leave
            off in the field.

endmenu
